    17 {}
#3 paragraph in #0 "Lines and scripts" {"style": Text("Heading 2")}
    17 {}
#4 paragraph in #0 "One line\u{2028}and the next, in one paragraph." {"style": Text("Body")}
    40 {}
#5 paragraph in #0 "Ελληνικά, русский, עברית, العربية, 中文." {"style": Text("Body")}
    38 {"bold": Bool(true), "size": Int(177800)}
#6 paragraph in #0 "Typed a word at a time" {"style": Text("Heading 3")}
    22 {}
#7 paragraph in #0 "Every word of this paragraph was typed as a step of its own, so the file's log runs past a hundred entries and holds a second snapshot. Opening it starts from that snapshot and replays the entries after it; its named versions start from the first snapshot instead. Undo takes back this whole run of typing at once, because each word continued the one before it, and Redo brings it back. A file M1 wrote must open in every later xWorks with the same text, the same formatting and the same history, or what people wrote with it was never really theirs to keep." {"style": Text("Body")}
    558 {}
